We derive an approximation for the resolvent of a fourth-order operator, specifically 
\begin{equation*}
  -\Delta \otimes \Delta + \frac{1}{\varepsilon} (\Delta \otimes \mathcal{A} + \mathcal{A} \otimes \Delta),
  \end{equation*}
where $\mathcal{A}$ is a positive, unbounded operator and $\varepsilon$ is a small positive parameter. This approximation is expressed in terms of the resolvents of $\mathcal{A}$ and $\Delta$, as well as the inverse of a certain difference operator. Our approach relies on the assumption that the eigenvalues of the difference operator are strictly positive.
